---
import { entities, relationships, typeLabel, formatRelation } from '../labs/memory/model';
---
<section class="memory-lab" data-memory-lab aria-label="Interactive knowledge graph lab">
  <div class="ml-guide" aria-label="Guided exploration">
    <div class="ml-guide-intro"><span class="eyebrow">A three-minute field trip</span><p>Try the graph. Leave a small edit. Bring it back.</p></div>
    <div class="ml-guide-steps">
      <button type="button" data-guide="find" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span> Find a connection <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></button>
      <button type="button" data-guide="inspect" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span> Inspect what it means <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></button>
      <button type="button" data-guide="edit" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span> Set this connection aside <i aria-hidden="true">↙</i></button>
    </div>
    <p class="ml-guide-note" data-guide-note>Start with panelforge. The lines show extracted build relationships. Choose a connected label or a connection in the list to inspect it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ml-workbench">
    <aside class="ml-directory" aria-labelledby="ml-directory-title">
      <div class="ml-panel-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Find an entity</p><h2 id="ml-directory-title">The index.</h2></div>
      <label class="ml-field">Search project or software<input type="search" data-entity-search placeholder="Try vue or panelforge" autocomplete="off" /></label>
      <label class="ml-field">Entity type<select data-entity-type aria-label="Entity type"><option value="all">All types</option><option value="project">Projects</option><option value="technology">Technology</option><option value="unknown">Unknown type</option></select></label>
      <p class="ml-directory-count" data-entity-count aria-live="polite">{entities.length} entity labels</p>
      <div class="ml-entity-list" data-entity-list>
        {entities.map((entity) => <button type="button" class="ml-entity" data-entity={entity.label} data-type={typeLabel(entity)} aria-pressed={entity.label === 'panelforge' ? 'true' : 'false'}><span>{entity.label}</span><small>{typeLabel(entity)}</small></button>)}
      </div>
      <p class="ml-empty" data-entity-empty hidden>No matching labels. Try a shorter search or another type.</p>
      <button type="button" class="ml-clear" data-clear-filter>Clear filters</button>
      <p class="ml-index-note">Original names, including versioned names and aliases. “Unknown” preserves an untyped record.</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="ml-map-panel">
      <label class="ml-quick-entity">Choose an entity<select data-focus-select aria-label="Choose an entity">{entities.map(entity => <option value={entity.label} selected={entity.label === 'panelforge'}>{entity.label} · {typeLabel(entity)}</option>)}</select></label>
      <div class="ml-map-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Follow its neighborhood</p><h2 data-focus-title>panelforge</h2><p data-focus-meta>Project · extracted historical relationships</p></div><span class="ml-map-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      <div class="ml-graph" data-graph aria-label="Focused relationships" role="group"></div>
      <div class="ml-selected-summary" data-selection-summary>
        <span class="eyebrow">Selected connection</span><p data-selection-tuple>panelforge → built_with → inertia-js</p>
        <div class="ml-selection-actions"><button type="button" data-map-inspect>Inspect its source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" data-map-edit>Set aside <span aria-hidden="true">↙</span></button></div>
        <div class="ml-inline-receipt" data-inline-receipt hidden><p data-inline-receipt-text role="status"></p><button type="button" data-inline-undo>Undo this edit <span aria-hidden="true">↶</span></button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ml-map-pagination"><p data-neighborhood-count aria-live="polite"></p><div><button type="button" data-neighborhood-prev aria-label="Previous connections">←</button><button type="button" data-neighborhood-next aria-label="Next connections">→</button></div></div>
      <p class="ml-map-hint">Arrowheads follow the stored direction. Select a connection to read it; choose an entity in the index to move the focus.</p>
      <details class="ml-connection-details" open><summary>Connections as a list <span data-relation-count></span></summary><div class="ml-connection-list" data-connection-list></div><p class="ml-empty" data-connection-empty hidden>No visible connections remain for this entity. Undo an edit, reset the sample, or choose another label.</p></details>
    </div>

    <aside class="ml-inspector" aria-labelledby="ml-inspector-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Read before you edit</p><h2 id="ml-inspector-title" tabindex="-1">A connection,<br /><em>in plain sight.</em></h2><button class="ml-return-map" type="button" data-return-map>← Back to the connection</button>
      <div class="ml-triple" data-triple><span class="ml-role">Subject</span><strong data-subject>panelforge</strong><span class="ml-predicate">↓ <code data-predicate>built_with</code></span><span class="ml-role">Object</span><strong data-object>inertia-js</strong></div>
      <p class="ml-meaning" data-meaning></p>
      <div class="ml-source" data-source hidden><span class="eyebrow">A checked source excerpt</span><blockquote data-source-quote></blockquote><p data-source-description></p><p class="ml-source-boundary">The excerpt supports reading the extracted relationship in its conversation context. It does not date every release or establish today's architecture.</p></div>
      <p class="ml-no-source" data-no-source>This tuple was exported from the real graph. An original source excerpt is not published for this connection.</p>
      <p class="ml-alias-note" data-alias-note></p>
      <div class="ml-edit-zone"><p>Practice curation by setting this connection aside. You can restore its exact before-state.</p><button type="button" class="ml-edit-button" data-set-aside>Set aside in this demo <span aria-hidden="true">↙</span></button><p class="ml-edit-status" data-edit-status></p><button type="button" class="ml-inspector-undo" data-inspector-undo hidden>Undo the last edit ↶</button></div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="ml-receipt" aria-labelledby="ml-receipt-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Your local edit trail</p><h2 id="ml-receipt-title">A change with a way back.</h2><p>These receipts describe only your interaction with this illustration. The exported sample stays intact.</p></div>
    <div class="ml-receipt-body"><div class="ml-receipt-toolbar"><span data-sample-count>{relationships.length} of {relationships.length} connections visible</span><div><button type="button" data-undo disabled>Undo last edit</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset sample</button></div></div><ol data-receipt-list class="ml-receipt-list"><li class="ml-receipt-empty">No edits yet. Select a connection and try setting it aside.</li></ol><p class="ml-live-message" data-live-message role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
  </section>
  <noscript><div class="ml-noscript"><p>The interactive map needs JavaScript. These are the original {relationships.length} exported connections, readable without it.</p><ul>{relationships.map((relation) => <li>{formatRelation(relation)}</li>)}</ul></div></noscript>
</section>
<script>
  import { mountMemoryLab } from '../labs/memory/controller';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-lab]').forEach(mountMemoryLab);
</script>
